/-!
# S2117: topological finite generation of G_L = Gal(Qbar_p / L)

Layer: **O**.  Consumer: S2116's input
  TopologicallyFinitelyGenerated U, U : Index p,
hence S2116's reduction of M2c to finite generation plus Nikolov-Segal.

## The target

S2116 reduced M2c to the statement that for every open subgroup
U of G_v = Gal(Qbar_p / Q_p), the group

  localGaloisGroup p U = Gal(Qbar_p / localField p U)

is topologically generated by finitely many elements:

  exists s : Finset (localGaloisGroup p U),
    (Subgroup.closure (s : Set _)).topologicalClosure = top.

This file reduces that statement, for *all* U, to the single case of the
absolute Galois group G_Qp = Gal(Qbar_p / Q_p) (canonically
localGaloisGroup p top up to the standard topological identification of
infinite Galois theory).  The reduction is unconditional and proved here:

* an open subgroup of a compact topological group topologically generated
  by finitely many elements is again topologically generated by finitely
  many elements (the topological Schreier argument, reduced to Mathlib's
  abstract Schreier lemma via density of L cap H in H);
* continuous surjective images preserve topological finite generation;
* the canonical group isomorphism
  localGaloisGroupEquiv p U : U ->* Gal(Qbar_p / L)
  is continuous for the subspace (Krull) topology on U and the Krull
  topology on the target.

The remaining missing theorem is the classical theorem

  PadicAbsoluteGaloisTopologicallyFinitelyGenerated :
    G_Qp is topologically generated by finitely many elements.

It is recorded as a Prop and is never assumed.  No target is changed.

## What is actually missing (honest)

Mathlib v4.32.2 has:

* Krasner's lemma, IsKrasner.of_completeSpace, specialised here to
  IsKrasner Q_p (PadicAlgCl p) (proved below as krasner_available);
* the infinite Galois correspondence and its Krull topology;
* abstract Schreier's lemma (Subgroup.fg_of_index_ne_zero);
* no local class field theory, no Demushkin/Shafarevich presentation of
  the maximal pro-p quotient, and no finite generation theorem for
  absolute Galois groups of local fields;
* no theory of verbal subgroups or uniform bounds (this is S2116's second
  input and is not used here).

The precise local-field finiteness statement that Krasner's lemma is
normally used to prove is recorded as FinitelyManyExtensionsOfDegree.
It is *necessary* but not sufficient for topological finite generation:
the profinite product of C_{p_n} over distinct primes has only finitely
many open subgroups of each index, but is not topologically finitely
generated.  Hence this file does not claim that finite extension
finiteness alone supplies S2116's input.  The actual first missing
statement is finite generation of G_Qp; the reduction below shows that this
single statement suffices for every G_L.  Its classical proof uses local
CFT/Demushkin theory,
which is absent from Mathlib and from the tree.

## Status

* Proved unconditionally: the open-subgroup reduction, the continuous
  transfer, continuity of the Galois identification, and the implication
  PadicAbsoluteGaloisTopologicallyFinitelyGenerated -> all U.
* Not proved: PadicAbsoluteGaloisTopologicallyFinitelyGenerated itself,
  and FinitelyManyExtensionsOfDegree.
* No sorry, admit, axiom, opaque or fabricated inhabitant.  The missing
  statements occur only as Prop-valued hypotheses.

## References

* H. Koch, on the structure of absolute Galois groups of p-adic fields;
  U. Jannsen and K. Wingberg, Die Struktur der absoluten Galoisgruppe
  p-adischer Zahlkoerper, Invent. Math. 70 (1982).
* J. Neukirch, A. Schmidt, K. Wingberg, Cohomology of Number Fields,
  Chapter VII (absolute Galois groups of local fields).
* J. Krasner, for finiteness of extensions of bounded degree; the Mathlib
  form is IsKrasner.of_completeSpace in Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Krasner.
* N. Nikolov, D. Segal, On finitely generated profinite groups I, Ann. of
  Math. 165 (2007), is not used here; the conditional consumer below takes it
  as an explicit hypothesis and does not close the target.
-/

noncomputable section
set_option maxHeartbeats 2000000
